  "slug": "biological-brain-types-006a",
  "summary": "Pretraining on over 160 million tandem mass spectra is now applied to dual-polarity molecular identification and structure elucidation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread in this set is improving confidence in compound annotation from tandem mass spectra. UltraMS is a dual-polarity foundation model pretrained on over 160 million tandem mass spectra, aimed at molecular identification and structure elucidation. Its distinguishing feature is large-scale pretraining on repository-wide metabolomics data, which the preprint frames as learning a molecular language for spectral interpretation. The other two preprints address different problems. MicroBioAgent is an LLM agent framework that converts biological queries into executable microbiome pipelines for 16S, shotgun, and assembly-based metagenomics. MSGFLEX is an end-to-end proteomics and metaproteomics pipeline built on MS-GF+ with XPECTRA XGBoost rescoring and QUANTIX protein quantification. Neither is a small-molecule annotation method. What is new in this set is the foundation-model approach to spectral annotation in UltraMS.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
